2759	   * RUNNING job in the DB" are always the same set — checking the local Map
2760	   * is exactly as correct as re-querying the DB for it, and far cheaper
2761	   * (zero extra round-trips on the hot path). It also sidesteps a subtler
2762	   * bug a DB-only check would have: two QUEUED jobs for the same serverId
2763	   * both present in the SAME claim batch could otherwise both pass an
2764	   * "is there already a RUNNING job for this serverId?" query (neither is
